### 12. `src/networking.c` - `writeToReplica` single block case (lines 2062-2072)

**Defect 24: Single block case doesn't handle partial write correctly (lines 2062-2072)**
```c
if (first_node == last_node) {
    replBufBlock *b = listNodeValue(first_node);
    c->nwritten = connWrite(c->conn, b->buf + c->ref_block_pos, bufpos - c->ref_block_pos);
    if (c->nwritten <= 0) {
        c->write_flags |= WRITE_FLAGS_WRITE_ERROR;
    }
    return;
}
```
If `connWrite` returns partial write (e.g., 30 of 64 bytes), `c->nwritten = 30`. Function returns. `postWriteToReplica` will be called and advance `c->ref_block_pos` by 30. Next call, `writeToReplica` called again, single block case again, writes remaining 34. This works correctly because `postWriteToReplica` advances the position.

But wait: `bufpos` is `c->io_last_bufpos` which was captured at offload time. If main thread added more data to the same block (increased `used`), `bufpos` is stale. The single block case writes up to `bufpos`, not `b->used`. This is by design (snapshot semantics). OK.

**Defect 25: `writeToReplica` doesn't check `bufpos > c->ref_block_pos` (line 2065)**
```c
c->nwritten = connWrite(c->conn, b->buf + c->ref_block_pos, bufpos - c->ref_block_pos);
```
If `bufpos <= c->ref_block_pos`, the length is 0 or negative (size_t underflow!). `connWrite` called with huge size. Crash or corruption.

**Concrete failure scenario:** Race condition: main thread sets `c->io_last_bufpos = 50` (captured `used`). IO thread starts, but before it runs, main thread calls `postWriteToReplica` which advances `c->ref_block_pos` to 60 (because previous write completed). Now `bufpos (50) < c->ref_block_pos (60)`. `bufpos - c->ref_block_pos` underflows to huge `size_t`. `connWrite` crashes or writes garbage.

This is a real race! The main thread advances `c->ref_repl_buf_node` and `c->ref_block_pos` in `postWriteToReplica`. The IO thread reads `c->io_last_bufpos` (snapshot at offload time) and `c->ref_block_pos` (current position). If a previous write completed and `postWriteToReplica` advanced `ref_block_pos` past the snapshot `io_last_bufpos`, the length calculation underflows.

